{"id":"u-b1664252-3d95-4dc6-bca8-33f25c8ef813","src":"community","title":"Viltrumite Physique","author":"Luke Trains","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/Xcfhkx-bigger-and-stronger-1","desc":"I suggest going 3 days on 1 day off. \n I wrote this program for myself to help me get a viltrumite level physique. This program has a heavy focus on hypertrophy with some compound movements added in to help increase general strength. EVERY movement should be done with strict form to properly target the desired muscle and reduce injury risk. 0 RIR should be technical failure. The last set of any given isolation exercise should be taken to failure, and feel free to use drop sets , rest pause, or myoreps, etc… at your discretion. Feel free to add in cable crunches or any other core work where you see fit (I do them at work). Always\nremember to warm up properly to reduce injury risk and ensure best performance. If you are lacking a given piece of equipment supplement with an exercise that has a similar movement pattern. Pull ups and dips can be done with assistance or added weight depending on your strength level. For best results this program should be done in a modest calorie surplus for maximum gains. This program should be run for 8-12 weeks focusing on progressively overloading each exercise. Feel free to make small adjustments if needed, just don’t switch up exercise variations before doing one for a minimum of 8 weeks. Have fun and don’t forget to hit full ROM.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":3,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-06-02T19:27:38.871Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest and Back","Shoulders and Arms","Legs","Chest and Back","Shoulders and Arms","Legs"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":6,"rpe":7,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":10}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Machine)","sets